&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world’s biggest financial problems. We’re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn’t a place for complacency, it’s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We’re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood&#39;s Crypto Legal team supports the company&#39;s onchain products, including Robinhood Chain, Robinhood Wallet, and Stock Tokens. The team partners with Product, Engineering, and Compliance across multiple business lines and jurisdictions to help these products launch responsibly and on schedule. We look for attorneys who are pragmatic, collaborative, and decisive.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Crypto Onchain Attorney, you will serve as product counsel for Robinhood&#39;s onchain products. You&#39;ll advise Product and Engineering teams on legal and regulatory considerations from early design through launch, and help structure go-to-market strategy across multiple jurisdictions. You will work closely with business partners throughout the Crypto organization to keep legal strategy consistent across the onchain product suite. This role has immediate, visible impact: you&#39;ll help shape how Robinhood develops onchain finance.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our New York, NY, Menlo Park, CA and Washington, DC office(s), with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as product counsel for Robinhood&#39;s onchain products, advising from concept through launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, and Compliance to evaluate legal and regulatory risk for new onchain features and multi-jurisdictional launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and edit commercial contracts in support of partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with legal and business partners to align legal strategy across the on-chain product suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and interpret crypto regulatory developments across jurisdictions, and translate them into practical guidance for Product and Engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop legal frameworks that support Robinhood&#39;s expansion into new onchain markets and products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a securities, derivatives, or financial services legal background, with experience moving into crypto-focused work, either in-house or at a law firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring 4+ years of relevant legal experience, including substantive work advising on self-custody wallets, decentralized exchanges, or tokenized assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable operating across jurisdictions where regulatory guidance is still developing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You explain legal and regulatory concepts clearly to non-legal partners in Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You balance legal risk with the pace of a fast-moving product organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience using the latest AI tooling for legal research and drafting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
