&lt;p&gt;The Performance Marketing team’s mission is to drive efficient, data-driven customer acquisition and growth for Robinhood by optimizing paid marketing investment across performance marketing channels like Google and Meta.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Performance marketing intern, you will own performance marketing campaigns across Google and paid social, and are responsible for the full-funnel performance of your campaigns.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Menlo Park, CA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and optimize day-to-day performance marketing campaigns across Google Ads and paid social platforms (Meta, TikTok, etc.), monitoring spend, pacing, and performance against targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze campaign data to identify trends, surface actionable insights, and recommend optimizations to improve CAC, ROAS, and other key performance metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain performance dashboards/reports to track campaign results and communicate findings to the broader marketing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct A/B tests on ad creative, targeting, and bidding strategies, and translate results into optimization recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with growth and analytics teams to ensure budget allocation and channel strategy are grounded in data, not assumptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
