&lt;p&gt;What if fans could be more than spectators? At Robinhood, we&#39;re building exactly that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Prediction Markets team is creating an entirely new asset class — one that lets customers engage with real-world events in dynamic, meaningful ways. This is one of the fastest-growing, most strategically important areas of the business, and the team is moving fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Product Designer for Sports, you&#39;ll own end-to-end design for the sports vertical within Prediction Markets — from early concept through live launch. You&#39;ll shape how fans experience sports trading flows, amplifier events, and engagement features tied to the biggest moments in sports. It&#39;s zero-to-one work with executive visibility, real stakes, and an audience that&#39;s genuinely excited about what you&#39;re building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with product managers, engineers, and operations partners — navigating ambiguity, moving with speed, and delivering experiences that connect sports culture with a new category of financial product. If you love the energy of game day and want to build something that&#39;s never existed before, this is the role for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA and New York, NY offices, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end design for the Sports vertical within Prediction Markets — from early concept through launch — taking full accountability for the quality and impact of every experience you ship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design sports trading flows, engagement features, and amplifier events tied to the biggest moments in sports, translating complex financial mechanics into experiences that feel intuitive and exciting for fans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product managers, engineers, and operations teams to define the right problems and drive high-priority initiatives from idea to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn ambiguous, first-of-its-kind challenges into clear, elegant product experiences — bringing structure to spaces where the playbook doesn&#39;t exist yet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incorporate feedback from senior leadership and stakeholders thoughtfully, iterating quickly without losing quality or vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product design experience with a strong portfolio that demonstrates both visual craft and end-to-end product thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing and launching new or early-stage products — you&#39;re comfortable with zero-to-one and know how to drive work forward without a fully defined path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to operate independently in ambiguous environments, synthesize feedback from multiple stakeholders, and make confident design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills — you work well with product, engineering, and operations partners and know how to align diverse perspectives toward a shared outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Figma and openness to integrating AI tools into your design workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine love for sports — whether you track stats, follow teams, or just live for the energy of game day. No formal sports design experience required; an appreciation for the fan experience is what matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
