&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world&#39;s biggest financial problems. We&#39;re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it&#39;s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We&#39;re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most designers ship features. On the Core Experience team, you shape the foundation that millions of people already use every day — rethinking how the app&#39;s most important surfaces are structured, not just how they look. Robinhood keeps growing into new products and markets, and this role makes sure the core experience scales right alongside it — a big, visible opportunity that lives or dies on the details. We ship constantly — this team moves in weeks, not quarters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Core Experience team rebuilds the foundation of core Robinhood products, taking an experimentation-first approach on some of our highest-visibility, most-used surfaces. We move quickly, test broadly, and iterate with purpose. Our culture values confidence, flexibility, and the ability to turn ambiguity into momentum — and we partner closely with Product to balance great user experience with real business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Designer on this team, you combine big-picture systems architecture with pixel-perfect craft. You&#39;ll own the core app shell — Home, Watchlists, Search, and beyond — rapidly generating and testing ideas across multiple product domains on surfaces that millions of users interact with every single day. You&#39;ll bring a strong point of view to your work and make the case for design decisions that involve real business trade-offs, including in conversations with executive leadership. The work is fast, visible, and consequential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Menlo Park, CA or New York, NY office(s), with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and hold the visual quality bar across the core app shell — including work you don&#39;t own directly — for surfaces millions of users see every day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly generate and test a broad range of incremental changes across the mobile app using an experimentation-first approach (A/B testing, concept sprints, iteration at speed).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for the core app shell — Home, Watchlists, Search, and the surfaces that connect them — across multiple product domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present design concepts directly to executive leadership with clarity and confidence, making the case for decisions that involve real business trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner tightly with Product Managers and engineers to deliver great experiences in fast-moving environments — with the autonomy to define the problem, not just solve it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing for consumer mobile applications on high-visibility surfaces, with a strong sense of how product structure and navigation hold up at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio that demonstrates exceptional visual craft and execution, from an in-house or agency background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real experience with experimentation methodologies — A/B testing, rapid concept generation, iterating based on data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence in your design decisions and the ability to navigate shifting requirements, advocate for your choices, and adapt without losing quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach to cross-functional relationships and genuine curiosity about emerging technologies, including AI tools in the design process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
